The orders library of `--decreases-orders` (`Std.Termination.Orders`) gains the multiset order, in the form of Huet and Oppen that VeriFast uses for its bags of call permission levels: `MultisetOf(r)` orders multisets over any relation `r` proved well-founded, so that one element may be exchanged for finitely many smaller ones. `MultisetGe` and `MultisetGt` define the order. The library proves it well-founded, with no new axiom, and transitive when `r` is, so `MultisetRel(r)` lets multiset orders nest. Its lemmas follow those of VeriFast's `termination.gh`, including both absorption laws of `>=` and `>`. It may be used in ordinary `decreases` clauses and, under `--modular-termination`, in `decreases {:global}` bounds, where the library's multiset functions and lemmas count as applications of the relation they are given. Programs without `--decreases-orders` are unaffected. See https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/211.
